    "probe_recall": 0.43902439024390244,
    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented by the function classes. I've marked each step as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state, persists, or logs).\n\n## 0. Authorization (endpoint guard)\n- **Validation** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. The whole endpoint requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role before any step runs; otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## 1. `RequireOwnerFields` (`validate`)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 reads the raw `@RequestBody` (before bean validation) and **normalizes the address in place** via `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n- **Validation** \u2014 rejects (400 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, listing offenders) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (*after* normalization), `city`, `telephone` is null/blank.\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 republishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n## 2. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`\n- **Validation** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is supplied and is after today's server date, reject 400 (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). Absent date passes.\n\n## 3. `ValidatePostcode`\n- **Validation** \u2014 postcode is optional; if present it must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in that range. Otherwise 400 (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Unknown city accepts any 4-digit code.\n\n## 4. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 rewrites `telephone` in place to E.164 form (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep leading `+`/country code, else assume `+61` and drop a single leading `0`).\n- **Validation** \u2014 if it cannot form valid E.164 (8\u201315 digits after `+`), reject 400 (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n\n## 5. `ValidateTelephoneCountryLength`\n- **Validation** \u2014 national-number length must match country code: `+61` \u2192 exactly 9 national digits, `+1` \u2192 exactly 10. Otherwise 400 (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n\n## 6. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 email optional; blank \u2192 set to `null`; otherwise trim and lower-case in place.\n- **Validation** \u2014 a present, non-blank email must match the syntactic pattern or reject 400 (`InvalidEmailException`).\n\n## 7. `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`\n- **Validation** \u2014 if the (normalized) email's domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), reject 400 (`DisposableEmailDomainException`). Null email skipped.\n\n## 8. `RejectCityAtCapacity`\n- **Validation** \u2014 counts existing owners in the requested city; if \u2265 50, reject 409 (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n## 9. `RejectDailyLimit`\n- **Validation** \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied date, else server date) rolled forward to a business day; if \u2265 100 existing owners already have that registration date, reject 429 (`DailyLimitExceededException`).\n\n---\n*From here on the steps run under `govern: [ transaction ]` \u2014 one write transaction that commits at the end.*\n\n## 10. `BuildOwner` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; sets `registrationDate` to the effective date rolled forward to a business day; publishes the `Owner`.\n\n## 11. `AssignNamesakeCount` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of *existing* owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive), before this owner is saved.\n\n## 12. `AssignCustomerCode` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode + first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over normalized-telephone + lastName).\n\n## 13. `AssignHousehold` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`.\n\n## 14. `RejectDuplicateIdentity` (transactional)\n- **Validation** \u2014 if any existing owner already has the same `householdId`, reject 409 (`DuplicateIdentityException`). Bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, or when `householdId` is null.\n\n## 15. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate=false` by default; if not a declared household member and there exists an owner with the same last name + postcode but a *different* E.164 telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = earliest matching owner's id. (Soft flag only; does not reject.)\n\n## 16. `AssignHouseholdSize` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing members sharing the `householdId` **plus 1** (this owner); 1 when no `householdId`.\n\n## 17. `SaveOwner` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns the id).\n\n## 18. `AuditOwnerCreated` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 logs an `AUDIT` info line with the new id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n## 19. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (transactional)\n- **Side-effect** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners already registered for today's business day), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n### Notes\n- **Validations that can reject** (in order): auth role \u2192 missing fields \u2192 future registration date \u2192 postcode \u2192 telephone E.164 \u2192 telephone national-length \u2192 disposable email domain \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429) \u2192 duplicate household identity (409).\n- **Ordering rationale baked in:** cheap body validations run before DB-touching checks; all mutations/persistence run inside the single `transaction` governance so the request commits once at the end. The telephone/email/address normalizations happen *before* the checks that depend on them (e.g. duplicate detection compares normalized values), and count-based assignments (`namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, duplicate checks) run before `SaveOwner` so the new owner isn't counted against itself.\n\nI did not modify anything."
